**BLUF:** Yes. The simplest approach is to use **one main domain** for your nonprofit and a **subdomain** for the marketplace:

- **Nonprofit:** `www.hopestand.org` (or `hopestand.org`)
- **Marketplace:** `marketplace.hopestand.org`

These are usually called **subdomains**, rather than alias links. You can host each as a separate website while keeping the single `hopestand.org` domain registration. Squarespace supports custom subdomains and can direct them either to another Squarespace site or to an external platform. 

## Recommended structure

| Purpose | Public link | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| HopeStand nonprofit site | `www.hopestand.org` | Make this your primary public-facing website. |
| HopeStand marketplace | `marketplace.hopestand.org` | A separate site/store with its own content, branding, and navigation. |
| Optional short redirect | `shop.hopestand.org` | Can redirect visitors to the marketplace link if you prefer a shorter name. |

You could also use `shop.hopestand.org` instead of `marketplace.hopestand.org`. I recommend **`marketplace.hopestand.org`** because it is immediately clear to visitors.

